# Proposal: remove the durable retry queue
The product accepts upload metadata before a slow external processor runs. Support sees duplicate
retry notifications; operations sees incidents where acknowledged jobs were lost after restarts.
The proposal removes the durable queue and always responds accepted after an in-memory enqueue.
The latency objective is p95 under 150 ms, but there are no current measurements. The agreed
contract promises accepted jobs survive a process restart. Reducing duplicates is desirable;
changing the durability promise is undecided. No implementation, experiments or external actions
are authorized. Analyze the real tensions, distinguish facts from assumptions and name a decisive
experiment that could resolve uncertainty without treating a preference as a settled decision.
